#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.50 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:9
msgid "A post-processing filter for \"diff --raw\" output has been introduced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:12
msgid ""
"\"git repack\" learned \"--combine-cruft-below-size\" option that controls "
"how cruft-packs are combined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:15
msgid ""
"TCP keepalive behaviour on http transports can now be configured by calling "
"cURL library."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:17
msgid "Incrementally updating multi-pack index files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:20
msgid ""
"\"git reflog\" learns \"drop\" subcommand, that discards the entire reflog "
"data for a ref."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:23
msgid ""
"A new userdiff driver for \".ini\" format configuration files has been "
"added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:26
msgid ""
"The job to coalesce loose objects into packfiles in \"git maintenance\" now "
"has configurable batch size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:30
msgid ""
"\"git clone\" still gave the message about the default branch name; this "
"message has been turned into an advice message that can be turned off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:33
msgid ""
"\"git rev-list\" learns machine-parsable output format that delimits each "
"field with NUL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:35
msgid "\"git maintenance\" learns a new task to expire reflog entries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:38
msgid ""
"Auth-related (and unrelated) error handling in send-email has been made more "
"robust."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:44
msgid ""
"Updating multiple references have only been possible in an all-or-nothing "
"fashion with transactions, but it can be more efficient to batch multiple "
"updates even when some of them are allowed to fail in a best-effort manner.  "
"A new \"best effort batches of updates\" mode has been introduced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:47
msgid ""
"\"git help --build-options\" reports SHA-1 and SHA-256 backends used in the "
"build."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:50
msgid ""
"\"git cat-file --batch\" and friends learned to allow \"--filter=\" to omit "
"certain objects, just like the transport layer does."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:53
msgid ""
"\"git blame --porcelain\" mode now talks about unblamable lines and lines "
"that are blamed to an ignored commit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:55
msgid "The build procedure installs bash (but not zsh) completion script."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:57
msgid "send-email has been updated to work better with Outlook's SMTP server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:60
msgid ""
"\"git diff --minimal\" used to give non-minimal output when its optimization "
"kicked in, which has been disabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:64
msgid ""
"\"git index-pack --fix-thin\" used to abort to prevent a cycle in delta "
"chains from forming in a corner case even when there is no such cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Make repository clean-up tasks that \"gc\" can do available to \"git "
"maintenance\" front-end."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:71
msgid ""
"Bundle-URI feature did not use refs recorded in the bundle other than normal "
"branches as anchoring points to optimize the follow-up fetch during \"git "
"clone\"; now it is told to utilize all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:74
msgid ""
"The `send-email` documentation has been updated with OAuth2.0 related "
"examples."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:78
msgid ""
"Two of the \"scalar\" subcommands that add a repository that hasn't been "
"under \"scalar\"'s control are taught an option not to enable the scheduled "
"maintenance on it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:81
msgid ""
"The userdiff pattern for shell scripts has been updated to cope with more "
"bash-isms."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:84
msgid ""
"\"git merge-tree\" learned an option to see if it resolves cleanly without "
"actually creating a result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:87
msgid ""
"The commit title in the \"rebase -i\" todo file are now prefixed with '#', "
"just like a merge commit being replayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:91
msgid ""
"\"git receive-pack\" optionally learns not to care about connectivity check, "
"which can be useful when the repository arranges to ensure connectivity by "
"some other means."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:93
msgid "\"git notes --help\" documentation updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:101
msgid ""
"A handful of built-in command implementations have been rewritten to use the "
"repository instance supplied by git.c:run_builtin(), its caller."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:103
msgid "\"git fsck\" becomes more careful when checking the refs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:108
msgid ""
"\"git fast-export | git fast-import\" learns to deal with commit and tag "
"objects with embedded signatures a bit better.  This is highly experimental "
"and the format of the data stream may change in the future without "
"compatibility guarantees."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:111
msgid ""
"The code paths to check whether a refname X is available (by seeing if "
"another ref X/Y exists, etc.) have been optimized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:113
msgid "First step of deprecating and removing merge-recursive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:118
msgid ""
"In protocol v2 where the refs advertisement is constrained, we try to tell "
"the server side not to limit the advertisement when there is no specific "
"need to, which has been the source of confusion and recent bugs.  Revamp the "
"logic to simplify."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:120
msgid "Update meson based build procedure for breaking changes support."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:122
msgid "Enable -Wunreachable-code for developer builds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:126
msgid ""
"Ensure what we write in assert() does not have side effects, and introduce "
"ASSERT() macro to mark those that cannot be mechanically checked for lack of "
"side effects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:129
msgid ""
"Give more meaningful error return values from block writer layer of the "
"reftable ref-API backend."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:133
msgid ""
"Make the code in reftable library less reliant on the service routines it "
"used to borrow from Git proper, to make it easier to use by external users "
"of the library."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:135
msgid "CI update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:138
msgid ""
"The object layer has been updated to take an explicit repository instance as "
"a parameter in more code paths."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:141
msgid "Some warnings from \"-Wsign-compare\" for builtin/rm.c have been squelched."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:144
msgid "A few traditional unit tests have been rewritten to use the clar framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:147
msgid "Some warnings from \"-Wsign-compare\" for pathspec.c have been squelched."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:151
msgid ""
"\"make test\" used to have a hard dependency on (basic) Perl; tests have "
"been rewritten help environment with NO_PERL test the build as much as "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:154
msgid ""
"Remove remnants of the recursive merge strategy backend, which was "
"superseded by the ort merge strategy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:156
msgid "Optimize the code to dedup references recorded in a bundle file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:159
msgid ""
"Update parse-options API to catch mistakes to pass address of an integral "
"variable of a wrong type/size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:164
msgid ""
"Since a call to repo_config() can be called with repo set to NULL these "
"days, a command that is marked as RUN_SETUP in the builtin command table "
"does not have to check repo with NULL before making the call."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:166
msgid "Overhaul of the reftable API."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:169
msgid "Reduce requirement for Perl in our documentation build and a few scripts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:172
msgid "The build procedure based on Meson learned to drive the benchmarking tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:174
msgid "Code clean-up for meson-based build infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:176
msgid "Add an equivalent to \"make hdr-check\" target to meson based builds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:178
msgid "Further code clean-up in the object-store layer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:180
msgid "Build performance fix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:183
msgid ""
"Teach \"git send-email\" to also consult `hostname -f` for mail domain to "
"compute the identity given to SMTP servers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:186
msgid ""
"The dependency on the_repository variable has been reduced from the code "
"paths in \"git replay\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:189
msgid ""
"Support to create a loose object file with unknown object type has been "
"dropped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:193
msgid ""
"The code path to access the \"packed-refs\" file while \"fsck\" is taught to "
"mmap the file, instead of reading the whole file into memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:195
msgid "Assorted fixes for issues found with CodeQL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:199
msgid ""
"Remove the leftover hints to the test framework to mark tests that do not "
"pass the leak checker tests, as they should no longer be needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:203
msgid ""
"When a stale .midx file refers to .pack files that no longer exist, we ended "
"up checking for these non-existent files repeatedly, which has been "
"optimized by memoizing the non-existence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:205
msgid "Build settings have been improved for BSD based systems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:209
msgid ""
"Newer version of libcURL detected curl_easy_setopt() calls we made with "
"platform-natural \"int\" when we should have used \"long\", which all have "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:214
msgid ""
"Tests that compare $HOME and $(pwd), which should be the same directory "
"unless the tests chdir's around, would fail when the user enters the test "
"directory via symbolic links, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:217
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.49"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:223
msgid ""
"The refname exclusion logic in the packed-ref backend has been broken for "
"some time, which confused upload-pack to advertise different set of refs.  "
"This has been corrected.  (merge 10e8a9352b tb/refs-exclude-fixes later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:227
msgid ""
"The merge-recursive and merge-ort machinery crashed in corner cases when "
"certain renames are involved.  (merge 3adba40858 "
"en/merge-process-renames-crash-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:232
msgid ""
"Certain \"cruft\" objects would have never been refreshed when there are "
"multiple cruft packs in the repository, which has been corrected.  (merge "
"08f612ba70 tb/multi-cruft-pack-refresh-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:236
msgid ""
"The xdiff code on 32-bit platform misbehaved when an insanely large context "
"size is given, which has been corrected.  (merge d39e28e68c "
"rs/xdiff-context-length-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:241
msgid ""
"GitHub Actions CI switched on a CI/CD variable that does not exist when "
"choosing what packages to install etc., which has been corrected.  (merge "
"ee89f7c79d kn/ci-meson-check-build-docs-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:246
msgid ""
"Using \"git name-rev --stdin\" as an example, improve the framework to "
"prepare tests to pretend to be in the future where the breaking changes have "
"already happened.  (merge de3dec1187 jc/name-rev-stdin later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:250
msgid ""
"An earlier code refactoring of the hash machinery missed a few required "
"calls to init_fn.  (merge d39f04b638 jh/hash-init-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:254
msgid ""
"A documentation page was left out from formatting and installation, which "
"has been corrected.  (merge ae85116f18 pw/build-breaking-changes-doc later "
"to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:259
msgid ""
"The bash command line completion script (in contrib/) has been updated to "
"cope with remote repository nicknames with slashes in them.  (merge "
"778d2f1760 dm/completion-remote-names-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:262
msgid ""
"\"Dubious ownership\" checks on Windows has been tightened up.  (merge "
"5bb88e89ef js/mingw-admins-are-special later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:266
msgid ""
"Layout configuration in vimdiff backend didn't work as advertised, which has "
"been corrected.  (merge 93bab2d04b fr/vimdiff-layout-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:269
msgid ""
"Fix our use of zlib corner cases.  (merge 1cb2f293f5 jk/zlib-inflate-fixes "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:272
msgid ""
"Fix lockfile contention in reftable code on Windows.  (merge 0a3dceabf1 "
"ps/mingw-creat-excl-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:277
msgid ""
"\"git-merge-file\" documentation source, which has lines that look like "
"conflict markers, lacked custom conflict marker size defined, which has been "
"corrected..  (merge d3b5832381 "
"pw/custom-conflict-marker-size-for-merge-related-docs later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:280
msgid ""
"Squelch false-positive from sparse.  (merge da87b58014 "
"dd/sparse-glibc-workaround later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:283
msgid ""
"Adjust to the deprecation of use of Ubuntu 20.04 GitHub Actions CI.  (merge "
"832d9f6d0b js/ci-github-update-ubuntu later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:286
msgid ""
"Work around CI breakage due to fedora base image getting updated.  (merge "
"8a471a663b js/ci-fedora-gawk later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:289
msgid ""
"A ref transaction corner case fix.  (merge b9fadeead7 "
"jt/ref-transaction-abort-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:292
msgid "Random build fixes.  (merge 85e1d6819f ps/misc-build-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:296
msgid ""
"\"git fetch [<remote>]\" with only the configured fetch refspec should be "
"the only thing to update refs/remotes/<remote>/HEAD, but the code was overly "
"eager to do so in other cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:299
msgid ""
"Incorrect sorting of refs with bytes with high-bit set on platforms with "
"signed char led to a BUG, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:302
msgid "\"make perf\" fixes.  (merge 1665f12fa0 pb/perf-test-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:305
msgid ""
"Doc mark-up updates.  (merge 5a5565ec44 ja/doc-reset-mv-rm-markup-updates "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:308
msgid ""
"Work around false positive from CodeQL checker.  (merge 0f558141ed "
"js/range-check-codeql-workaround later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:312
msgid ""
"\"git log --{left,right}-only A...B\", when A and B does not share any "
"common ancestor, now behaves as expected.  (merge e7ef4be7c2 "
"mh/left-right-limited later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:316
msgid ""
"Document the convention to disable hooks altogether by setting the hooksPath "
"configuration variable to /dev/null.  (merge 1b2eee94f1 ds/doc-disable-hooks "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:320
msgid ""
"Make sure outage of third-party sites that supply P4, Git-LFS, and JGit we "
"use for testing would not prevent our CI jobs from running at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:323
msgid ""
"Various build tweaks, including CSPRNG selection on some platforms.  (merge "
"cdda67de03 rj/build-tweaks later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:326
msgid ""
"Developer support fix..  (merge 32b74b9809 js/git-perf-env-override later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:329
msgid ""
"Fix for scheduled maintenance tasks on platforms using launchctl.  (merge "
"eb2d7beb0e jh/gc-launchctl-schedule-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:333
msgid ""
"Update to arm64 Windows port (part of which had been reverted as it broke "
"builds for existing platforms, which may need to be redone in future "
"releases)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:337
msgid ""
"hashmap API clean-up to ensure hashmap_clear() leaves a cleared map in a "
"reusable state.  (merge 9481877de3 en/hashmap-clear-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:343
msgid ""
"\"git mv a a/b dst\" would ask to move the directory 'a' itself, as well as "
"its contents, in a single destination directory, which is a contradicting "
"request that is impossible to satisfy. This case is now detected and the "
"command errors out.  (merge 974f0d4664 ps/mv-contradiction-fix later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:347
msgid ""
"Further refinement on CI messages when an optional external software is "
"unavailable (e.g. due to third-party service outage).  (merge 956acbefbd "
"jc/ci-skip-unavailable-external-software later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:350
msgid ""
"Test result aggregation did not work in Meson based CI jobs.  (merge "
"bd38ed5be1 ps/ci-test-aggreg-fix-for-meson later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:353
msgid ""
"Code clean-up around stale CI elements and building with Visual Studio.  "
"(merge a7b060f67f js/ci-buildsystems-cleanup later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:357
msgid ""
"\"git add 'f?o'\" did not add 'foo' if 'f?o', an unusual pathname, also "
"existed on the working tree, which has been corrected.  (merge ec727e189c "
"kj/glob-path-with-special-char later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.50.0.adoc:362
msgid ""
"The fallback implementation of open_nofollow() depended on open(\"symlink\", "
"O_NOFOLLOW) to set errno to ELOOP, but a few BSD derived systems use "
"different errno, which has been worked around.  (merge f47bcc3413 "
"cf/wrapper-bsd-eloop later to maint)."
